# Passes everything, /ws included, to the server, which sends the page's headers and caching rules itself.
# Caddy adds the X-Forwarded-For that the server needs to tell its clients apart. Put your own domain in
# place of whist.example.org, with an A record that points at this machine.
whist.example.org {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
